---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import QuickUpdate from '../components/QuickUpdate.astro';
import { getCurrentWeek } from '../lib/content.mjs';
import { url } from '../lib/markdown.mjs';
import { SITE } from '../config.mjs';

const week = getCurrentWeek();
---
<Base title="Log progress">
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="hero-text">
      <span class="label">Owner only · progress logging</span>
      <h1 class="page-title">Log progress</h1>
      <p class="lede">Entries are committed straight to the <a href={url('/progress-log/')}>progress log</a> in the repo. Only a browser unlocked with {SITE.owner}'s GitHub token can save one.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="split">
    <div class="side" style="flex: 1 1 420px; max-width: 560px">
      <QuickUpdate week={week?.n} mode="page" />
    </div>
    <div class="grow prose">
      <h3 id="one-time-setup">One-time setup (per device)</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>On GitHub open <b>Settings → Developer settings → Personal access tokens → Fine-grained tokens → Generate new token</b>.</li>
        <li><b>Repository access:</b> <em>Only select repositories</em> → <code>{SITE.repo}</code>.</li>
        <li><b>Permissions:</b> <em>Contents → Read and write</em>. Nothing else is needed.</li>
        <li>Pick an expiry (for example 1 year), generate, copy the token and paste it here.</li>
      </ol>
      <h3 id="how-it-works">How it works</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Saving adds your entry to the top of <code>content/progress-log.md</code> as a normal commit. That push rebuilds the site and refreshes the README.</li>
        <li>The token is stored only in this browser and sent only to <code>api.github.com</code>. It's limited to this one repository's files.</li>
        <li>Visitors don't see the log form or the "+ log progress" button. Without your token, nothing can be written.</li>
        <li>On a shared computer, untick <em>remember on this device</em>, or press <b>lock</b> when done.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="callout callout-warning"><p class="callout-title">Lost device or leaked token?</p><p>Revoke it under GitHub → Settings → Developer settings → Fine-grained tokens. It stops working immediately.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
